node_modules/
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/*.sqlite
data/master.json
data/master.key
data/exports/
data/tls-*.pem
/* a test boots its own throwaway store (test/<name>.db) and deletes it on exit; a
   killed run leaves the file behind, so these are never committed either */
test/*.db
test/*.db-wal
test/*.db-shm
.luxora.pid
.luxora *.pid
server.log
/tmp
.DS_Store
/* the compiled single source of truth is DERIVED from the corpora + the authored
   _registry/*.json inputs: it is sealed with a per-deployment key (data/registry.json)
   and re-compiles deterministically, so the artifacts are never committed. The
   sources are the authority; the seal is reproducible, verifiable, not stored. */
_registry/canonical.json
_registry/canonical.lxr
data/registry.json
